    "security": "No independently validated exploit in owned scope. Callback and custom-attribute extension code is trusted application code. Lifecycle omission can bypass application checks put in constructors, but exploitability was not established. Request and parameter trust boundaries delegated.",
    "performance": "Reviewed metadata/sequence reuse and ownership. Existing availability-performance design remains separate. No numerical optimization or speedup claimed; no redundant benchmark added for the correctness finding.",
    "filtered_candidates": [
      "Make+Proxy fresh arguments are already instantiated once per resolution in both declaration orders; existing lifecycle test covers the concern.",
      "Custom composition rules disable the immutable-plan cache; mutable-rule behavior was not treated as stale cached logic.",
      "Native proxy wrapper and backing-object identities are intentionally distinct. A WeakMap keyed by backing identity is not a valid assertion of transparent wrapper state.",
      "Property name collisions across private ancestors are represented with declaring-class identity and have existing parity coverage.",
      "Standalone directly constructed internal metadata policy questions are already tracked; no unsupported API assumption was converted into a bug fix."
    ]
